        "content": "# Quick Build: Ultra-Performant JSON Validation Script\n\n**Request**: Add a JSON validation script that's ultra performant\n**Scope**: Small\n**Created**: 2026-03-08\n\n## Summary\n\nCreate an ultra-performant JSON validation module for the Bun/TypeScript project. The implementation will use a hand-rolled recursive descent validation approach that avoids unnecessary object allocation and leverages Bun's native performance. The module will validate JSON strings, provide detailed error reporting with position info, and support schema-like type checking for common patterns.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n- **No external dependencies**: Follows project pattern of using only Bun built-ins\n- **Streaming character-by-character validation**: Avoids parsing into objects (faster than `JSON.parse` for validation-only use cases)\n- **TypeScript strict mode**: Consistent with project conventions\n- **Co-located tests**: Following `*.test.ts` pattern\n\n## Files Affected\n\n- `src/json-validator.ts` (NEW) - Core validation module\n- `src/json-validator.test.ts` (NEW) - Comprehensive tests\n- `src/index.ts` (MODIFY) - Add CLI integration for JSON validation\n\n## Tasks\n\n### Task 1: Create core JSON validation module\n- **ID**: task-1\n- **Status**: pending\n- **File**: `src/json-validator.ts`\n- **Description**: Implement an ultra-performant JSON validator that validates JSON strings character-by-character without allocating intermediate objects. Should include:\n  - `validateJson(input: string): ValidationResult` - Main validation function\n  - `ValidationResult` type with `valid: boolean`, `errors: ValidationError[]`\n  - `ValidationError` type with `message: string`, `position: number`, `line: number`, `column: number`\n  - Support all JSON types: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null\n  - Handle edge cases: unicode escapes, nested structures, trailing commas detection, duplicate key detection\n  - Use performance optimizations: charCodeAt instead of charAt, pre-computed lookup tables, minimal allocations, early exits\n\n### Task 2: Create comprehensive tests\n- **ID**: task-2\n- **Status**: pending\n- **File**: `src/json-validator.test.ts`\n- **Description**: Write thorough tests using Bun's test runner covering:\n  - Valid JSON: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, null, nested structures\n  - Invalid JSON: trailing commas, single quotes, unquoted keys, truncated input, invalid escapes\n  - Edge cases: empty input, deeply nested structures, large numbers, unicode\n  - Error reporting: correct position/line/column in error messages\n  - Performance: validate that large JSON strings complete within reasonable time\n\n### Task 3: Integrate with CLI entry point\n- **ID**: task-3\n- **Status**: pending\n- **File**: `src/index.ts`\n- **Description**: Add JSON validation capability to the CLI entry point:\n  - When called with `--validate-json <file>`, read and validate the file\n  - When called with `--validate-json -`, read from stdin\n  - Print validation results with colored output (valid/invalid + errors)\n  - Maintain existing greeting functionality as default behavior\n"
